# OnlineSafety.cshtml

```cshtml id="k4x2mz"
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Online Safety";
}

<section class="why-section">

    <div class="section-heading">

        <h1>🔐 Online Safety</h1>

        <p>
            Learn how to stay safe while using digital devices and online services.
        </p>

    </div>


    <div class="feature-grid">

        <!-- Step 1 -->
        <div class="feature-card">

            <div class="feature-icon">🔑</div>

            <h3>Step 1: Protect Your Password</h3>

            <p>
                Use a strong password and do not share it with other people.
                Avoid using simple passwords that are easy to guess.
            </p>

        </div>


        <!-- Step 2 -->
        <div class="feature-card">

            <div class="feature-icon">🔢</div>

            <h3>Step 2: Never Share OTP or PIN</h3>

            <p>
                Never share your OTP, UPI PIN, ATM PIN or password with anyone,
                even if they claim to be from a bank or company.
            </p>

        </div>


        <!-- Step 3 -->
        <div class="feature-card">

            <div class="feature-icon">⚠️</div>

            <h3>Step 3: Avoid Suspicious Links</h3>

            <p>
                Do not click unknown links received through messages, emails
                or social media. They may lead to unsafe websites or scams.
            </p>

        </div>


        <!-- Step 4 -->
        <div class="feature-card">

            <div class="feature-icon">📞</div>

            <h3>Step 4: Beware of Online Fraud</h3>

            <p>
                Be careful of callers asking for bank details, OTPs, passwords
                or money. Do not provide personal information to unknown people.
            </p>

        </div>


        <!-- Step 5 -->
        <div class="feature-card">

            <div class="feature-icon">🌐</div>

            <h3>Step 5: Use Trusted Websites</h3>

            <p>
                Use trusted and official websites for banking, shopping,
                healthcare and government services.
            </p>

        </div>


        <!-- Step 6 -->
        <div class="feature-card">

            <div class="feature-icon">👨‍👩‍👧</div>

            <h3>Step 6: Ask for Help</h3>

            <p>
                If you receive a suspicious message or face an unusual
                situation online, ask a trusted family member or trainer
                for help.
            </p>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- Important Safety Tip -->

    <div class="about-section">

        <h2>🛡️ Important Safety Tip</h2>

        <p>
            Remember: banks and genuine organizations do not normally ask
            you to share your OTP, PIN or password. When in doubt, stop
            the activity and ask someone you trust.
        </p>

        <a asp-controller="Home"
           asp-action="Learn"
           class="btn btn-primary-custom">

            ← Back to Learning Modules

        </a>

    </div>

</section>
